<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Debre Berhan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Debre Berhan is a town in the highlands of North Shewa, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a>. It was founded by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zara-yaqob">Zara Yaqob</a> in the 1450s after a miraculous light was said to have appeared there, and served as his capital. In the 19th century it was again a royal residence of the kings of Shewa.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/debre-berhan.jpg" alt="Debre Berhan" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ji-Elle · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Debre_Birham_(3).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
